No licence for reconstructed code (SPDX: LicenseRef-reconstructed)
------------------------------------------------------------------
Code reconstructed from the retail game is not licensed by the Izanagi
contributors, because it is not theirs to license. That is code decompiled or
translated from the retail executable, from its statically linked middleware
(CRI, RenderWare) or from its runtime libraries. The text of this carve-out is
LICENSES/LicenseRef-reconstructed.txt. It applies to:

  overrides/                     decompiled replacements for retail functions
  drafts/                        unreviewed machine decompilations of retail functions
  src/cri/                       CRI middleware functions translated from the retail asm
  src/platform/ee_libm.c         the retail float libm cores (fdlibm), translated
  src/platform/ee_dlibm.c        the retail double libm cores (fdlibm), translated
  src/platform/ps2_fpbit.c       the retail soft-float cores (GCC fp-bit), translated
  src/platform/ee_heap.c         the retail newlib allocator (dlmalloc), translated
  src/platform/rw_rtanim.c       RenderWare RtAnim functions, translated
  src/platform/rw_rtanim_record.c
  src/platform/rw_skytran.c      the RenderWare sky driver's VU0 multiplies, translated
  src/platform/rw_device_register.c, rw_image_stream.c, rw_normalize2.c,
  rw_normalize3.c, rw_p2_stalac.c, rw_plugin_constructors.c,
  rw_skin_callees.c              RenderWare functions transcribed from the retail asm

These files carry an SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-reconstructed line,
except overrides/: the build splices those files byte for byte into the decomp
mirror, whose edits config/mirror_contracts.json pins, so REUSE.toml marks
them instead. The same applies to any other code in this repository that
reproduces or translates code of the retail executable, wherever it lives.

The decompilation itself, Raikaru/Persona4-Decompilation, is a separate
repository used as the decomp/ submodule. It has its own terms, and it is not
covered by this repository's licence.

